            <ArticleTitle>When an athlete can't catch his breath.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>454-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Don't rely on self-reported symptoms to diagnose exercise-induced bronchoconstriction (EIB). Indirect testing is the best way to diagnose EIB in patients who do not have underlying asthma. Short-acting beta2-agonists should be first-line management in EIB.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
